Oolite 1.93.1 for AmigaOS 3 on GFOS
===================================

Oolite is a space trading and combat game in the spirit of Elite: fly
between star systems, trade, fight pirates or become one, and dock at the
spinning stations. This is Oolite 1.93.1 on GFOS and AmiCradle, built for
the 68040, drawing with OpenGL through GFOpenGPU and running its game
scripts on javascript.library.

Version @VERSION@, a release candidate.

Requirements
------------

- GFOS (AmigaOS 3.2) on AmiCradle: the AC090 68040 with its JIT, on an
  x86-64 PC or a Raspberry Pi 5 / CM5, with GFOpenGPU (OpenGL 3.1 or
  newer on the host). A real 68040 or 68060 is far too slow for it.
- 768 MB of free memory; the game uses about 450 MB in flight.
- About 300 MB of disk.
- javascript.library 2.0, its engine and SDL3.module come in the drawer's
  Libs drawer; Oolite-Start puts them in front of LIBS: while the game
  runs, so nothing is copied into your system.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive anywhere, then double-click Install-Oolite beside the
Oolite drawer. It asks where Oolite goes (DH2:Ports, or Work:Games, by
default).

Playing
-------

- Double-click Oolite-Start. The title screen takes about 20 seconds.
  Oolite's own messages go to T:oolite.out.
- Start a new commander, or load one. Saved games are in
  ENVARC:oolite-saves.
- Oolite's keys are the standard ones: F1 launches from the station,
  the cursor keys steer, W and S set the speed, and F5 to F8 show the
  status, chart, system data and market screens. The full list is on
  oolite.space.

How fast it is
--------------

- AmiCradle on an x86-64 PC: about 40 frames a second in flight.
- Raspberry Pi 5 / CM5: about 33 at the title and 16 in flight at
  1280x720. Starting a new commander takes about 100 seconds.

What this build leaves out
--------------------------

- On the Pi's OpenGL 3.1 the HUD's scanner and compass draw only in part.
- The window's size comes from the game's defaults: oolite.plist in
  ENVARC:gnustep/defaults is not read back yet.
- Loading a saved game and ending a game reload the ship data, which
  takes 45 to 70 seconds.
- Memory grows slowly while the game is left docked (about 130 MB in
  three hours).
- Sound has not been checked in this release candidate.

This is a release candidate. It runs on AmiCradle's lab and on a CM5.
Report problems at https://github.com/amigagfosports/amigaoolite.

